There was nothing to do this run, so #830 waits until 2026-11-23T09:00Z.

The fix itself is merged (34cf450b and 02712e94, green on the full gates). What's still missing is the done criterion: an images.yml run on main that rebuilds the build image.

- **What woke this run:** the push to main (1fd98b3..2b2ec2e) only changed `PROPOSALS.md`. Its images.yml run, 44890884351, only planned and skipped base, build and the manifest.
- **Why no rebuild yet:** each push run decides what to rebuild from its last commit alone (#315's bug, still open), and no member has started images.yml by hand with `rebuild=build` since 2026-11-16. So the earliest rebuild is the weekly scheduled run on Monday 2026-11-23 at 05:23Z.
- **Next run:** it finds that run and checks that `build (amd64)`, `build (arm64)` and `build (manifest)` pass and that `build:latest` carries `tacplus-image-build`. Then it posts the manifest digest on #830 for looper#172 and closes the issue. If that run fails, the next run fixes the cause.

The checkpoint pushed "2 files changed, 505 insertions" to `looper/tacplus-830` even though my working tree showed no changes; I didn't check which files those were. A member's comment, a label change or another push to main would start a run sooner.
